Hmm. I'm not actually convinced genocide needs any more nerfing than
it already got [1], but the idea of making foos of genocide a bit
harder to get is an interesting one.

As it stands right now, geno scrolls aren't terribly hard to come by.
They're generated randomly, and, in my experience, aren't all that
rare. (It might just be my imagination, but I think I trip over them a
little less often in Spork, but I haven't source-dove to double-check
yet.) And once you've seen one - or if you're a lucky wizard, even if
you haven't - the only real factor limiting how many shots you get is
the number of markers you find and how badly you need those markers
for something else. So, making geno a little harder to do by vesting
it in an item that a player can't just create arbitrarily many of is
an idea that might be worth exploring. I'm not sure what kind of item
this would be, though - a wand seems a little odd, even if it always
kabooms when you recharge it, and Yet Another tool seems like a weird
choice. I suppose a workable idea might be to make throne genocide
considerably more probable and then dike out the scroll, but, I'm not
sure. Like I said, it's something worth thinking about, but I'm not
sure geno actually needs to be nerfed.

Another workaround, for the L case specifically, might be to add more
Ls, some more or less pesky than the existing ones, but that's a band-
aid.

[1] - the current blessed-geno nerf is a good one, IMHO. Makes it a
bit more scroll-intensive to remove all of the most pesky monsters
without removing the utility of a blessed scroll. Also creates an
interesting tradeoff - it's no longer a no-brainer to bless the
scroll, if you want to make sure that one specific kind of irritating
monster gets whacked.


